# NEGATIVE TEST: the header-name value opens a quoted string that is never
# closed before end-of-line. Blocks in HMR are keyword-delimited (not
# indentation-sensitive), so this is now a *lexical* error: the ANTLR lexer
# cannot match a STRING token and reports an invalid-character error, which the
# parser collects via its error listener instead of crashing.
sip-manipulation BadString
        header-rule
                name  x
                header-name  "From
